 happened\"},{\"b\":\"[340,965][1012,1051]\",\"a11y\":\"Draw a loop and finish where you began, or end your line on another line. Two gold sparkles where the ends meet mean a new cell was made. It keeps the paint of the cell it was cut from, so it looks the same until you give it a paint of its own with the Bucket, or turn on Numbers in Layers to see its number.\",\"c\":[{\"b\":\"[918,1009][971,1031]\",\"a11y\":\"Bucket\",\"rid\":\"guide:bucket\"},{\"b\":\"[490,1031][540,1051]\",\"a11y\":\"Layers\",\"rid\":\"guide:layers\"}]},{\"b\":\"[340,1065][1012,1130]\",\"a11y\":\"If you\u2019d rather each new piece took its color from your photo, turn on Color from Photo. Every piece a line cuts off then takes the photo\u2019s color under it. If the picture already has a paint close to that color, the piece gets that paint; if not, a new paint is added.\"},{\"b\":\"[340,1144][988,1186]\",\"a11y\":\"A line that doesn\u2019t close anything off stays as ink. It shows in the finished picture, but the paint on both sides of it is still one cell.\"},{\"b\":\"[340,1210][380,1231]\",\"a11y\":\"Snap\"},{\"b\":\"[340,1245][999,1353]\",\"a11y\":\"Snap is on to start with. It moves an end that stops just short of a line, or runs a little past it, onto the line, and closes a loop whose end comes back near its start. Near means about 10 points on the screen, whatever the zoom (20 for an end heading straight at the picture\u2019s edge), so zoom in to end a line close to another without joining it. With Snap off, an end joins a line only when it all but touches it.\"}]}]},{\"b\":\"[999,834][1029,1344]\",\"a11y\":\"Vertical scroll bar, 3 pages\",\"txt\":\"0%\",\"val\":\"0%\",\"c\":[{\"b\":\"[1026,837][1029,1062]\"}]},{\"b\":\"[999,834][1029,1344]\",\"a11y\":\"Vertical scroll bar, 3 pages\",\"txt\":\"0%\",\"val\":\"0%\",\"c\":[{\"b\":\"[1026,837][1029,1062]\"}]}]}]}]}]}]},{\"b\":\"[0,0][1032,1376]\",\"a11y\":\"Toolbar\",\"rid\":\"Toolbar\",\"c\":[{\"b\":\"[0,0][1032,1376]\"}]}]}]},{\"b\":\"[0,0